  "bug_report_content": "Title: MultivariateNormalDistribution.density(double[]) returns wrong value when the dimension is odd\nType: Bug | Priority: Critical | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nTo reproduce:\n{code}\nAssert.assertEquals(0.398942280401433, new MultivariateNormalDistribution(new double[]{0}, new double[][]{{1}}).density(new double[]{0}), 1e-15);\n{code}\n\nComments:\n\n[Gilles Sadowski]: Corrected in revision 1433367.\n\nThanks a lot for the report and fix!\n\nA few weeks, Thomas wondered why using \"0.5 * x\" instead of \"x / 2\". That's an excellent reason... Unfortunately that instance slipped through my scanner :(.\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: Closing issue as version 3.2 has been released on 2013-04-06.",
